<title>UK: Sullom Voe oil liftings rise one third in week.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe oil liftings rise one third in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brent Blend crude oil loadings from Britain's Sullom Voe terminal rose to 750,992 tonnes in the week to June 10, from 550,207 tonnes the previous week, Shetland Islands Council said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Nearly half the liftings went to the U.S. Gulf Coast in an Ultra Large Crude Carrier (ULCC), with around 40 percent going to refineries in the U.K. and the balance to northwest Europe.</p>
